<BaseLayout title="Data & Coverage — BarcodeNest" description="How BarcodeNest indexes and normalises grocery product data, with transparent coverage and Open Food Facts attribution." current="data">
  <header class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">About the data</div><h1>A clearer service layer for open product information.</h1><p class="lede">BarcodeNest validates identifiers, indexes product records, normalises selected fields, and exposes consistent API responses—with provenance kept visible.</p></div></header>
  <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="content-grid">
    <article class="content-block"><h3>Indexed, not proxied</h3><p>Customer lookups query BarcodeNest’s own indexed database. They do not call Open Food Facts live during each request.</p></article>
    <article class="content-block"><h3>Canonical identifiers</h3><p>Accepted barcodes are validated and mapped to a zero-padded GTIN-14 identity to help equivalent representations resolve consistently.</p></article>
    <article class="content-block"><h3>Structured responses</h3><p>Product identity, product attributes and source metadata are separated into a predictable response schema.</p></article>
    <article class="content-block"><h3>Visible provenance</h3><p>Responses can identify the source and source record. BarcodeNest does not claim ownership of third-party product data.</p></article>
  </div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container metric-row"><div class="big-metric">4.2M<span>+</span></div><div><div class="eyebrow">Current coverage</div><h2>Global, with stronger European depth.</h2><p class="lede">The current index contains more than 4.2 million grocery products. Around 76% of current records have an image, but availability varies and an image URL may still be absent for any given lookup.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="narrow"><div class="eyebrow">Open Food Facts</div><h2>Attribution and reuse.</h2><p>BarcodeNest’s initial grocery data is derived from <a href="https://world.openfoodfacts.org/" rel="external"><u>Open Food Facts</u></a>, a collaborative open database. BarcodeNest provides an indexed and normalised API/service layer; it does not own Open Food Facts data and is not endorsed by Open Food Facts.</p><p>The Open Food Facts database is made available under the <a href="https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/" rel="external"><u>Open Database License (ODbL)</u></a>, which includes attribution and share-alike requirements. Individual database contents and product images can have separate licensing considerations. Review the current <a href="https://world.openfoodfacts.org/terms-of-use" rel="external"><u>Open Food Facts terms</u></a> for your particular reuse.</p><div class="callout">Source attribution is carried in BarcodeNest API responses where available. No partnership or endorsement is implied.</div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="narrow"><div class="eyebrow">Coverage limits</div><h2>What to expect.</h2><p class="lede">Coverage is not universal. Field completeness varies by product, source, market and geography. Names and brands are more common than ingredients, allergens, nutrition or images, and data can be incomplete or out of date.</p><p>Evaluate the API with barcodes representative of your users, regions and categories. For questions about a particular use case, email <a href="mailto:support@barcodenest.com"><u>support@barcodenest.com</u></a>.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
